# covered by MIT; see LICENSE and DATA_LICENCE.md.
license: OGL-UK-3.0
license-url: 'https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-04'
keywords:
  - deprivation
  - IMD
  - Indices of Deprivation 2025
  - Sub-ICB Location
  - SICBL
  - Integrated Care Board
  - England
  - health inequalities
abstract: >-
  Population-weighted average Index of Multiple Deprivation 2025 scores for
  England's 106 Sub-ICB Locations, covering the overall IMD, all seven domains,
  both supplementary indices and all six sub-domains, across four Sub-ICB
  boundary years (2023-2026). Scores only; no ranks or deciles. Uses MHCLG's
  "Average score" higher-area summary measure with the index-specific
  population weighting set out in the Indices of Deprivation 2025 Technical
  Report (para 3.8.8). MHCLG publish higher-area summaries for local
  authorities, ICBs and other geographies but not for Sub-ICB Locations, which
  is the gap this fills. The method was checked by repeating the same
  calculation for Integrated Care Boards and both local authority tiers and
  reproducing MHCLG's published summaries across 6,040 comparisons.
references:
  - type: report
    title: English Indices of Deprivation 2025
    authors:
      - name: >-
          Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government
    year: 2025
